[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   step_088: Galactic-tide insertion on the resident population --
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   maintenance and regeneration tests.
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   step_070 measured the tide's contribution to the transit channel
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   (~1e-9 deg, null).  The resident side carries a different question:
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   the Galactic tide is the standard "no new physics" mechanism invoked
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   for outer-system apsidal structure, so the decisive test is whether
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   the tide can *maintain* the observed varpi cluster or *regenerate*
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   one from an isotropic start.  This step inserts the same epoch-fixed
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   inertial tide tensor used in step_070 (Kx=+OmG^2, Ky=-OmG^2,
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   Kz=-4 pi G rho) into the step_066 secular harness -- the 44 detached
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   TNOs (a>150, q>30, cc<=3) integrated 20 Myr under Sun+giants -- via
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   Strang-split velocity kicks.
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   Three realizations:
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   tide_observed   : real catalogue varpi + giants + tide
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   -> does the tide hold or disperse R_varpi?
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   tide_scrambled  : initial varpi randomized (a,e,i,Om fixed, w reset)
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   -> does the tide *create* varpi concentration, and
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   if so at what direction?
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   tide_p9_med     : real varpi + giants + tide + BB21 median P9
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   -> does tide+perturber jointly confine?
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   Diagnostics per model: sigma(dvarpi/dt) and dispersal time (as 066);
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   R_varpi(t); the final mean varpi direction; and a restoring-torque
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   test against the tide's own ecliptic libration directions (the
[2026-09-20 11:54:11 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 088]   galactic-plane points l=90/270 deg, the tide's stationary loci).
